{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790257450,"nonce":"ku8InM7D8OmjvQFmUx8S/5R1Py4=","title":"Issue4886 lost: a field initializer typed an anon-returning method as Dynamic","message":"52585dd3 made an Array\u003cDynamic\u003e element load as a box pointer. Issue4886 then went PASS -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER (`f: expected false`), because its array is not really Array\u003cDynamic\u003e:\n\n    extern inline function get() { var intStruct = { i: 0 }; return intStruct; }\n    var a = [get(), get(), get()];   // field initializer\n    b = a[0] == a[1];                // Haxe: false\n\nThe field initializer is typed during class registration, before get()'s body infers its return type. The pre-registration pass (classes.rs anonymous_return_type_from_ast) handled `return {...}` but not `return v` for `var v = {...}`, so the call decayed to Dynamic, and the elements (raw anon pointers, not boxes) went to haxe_dynamic_equals / haxe_dynamic_field: `a[0] == a[1]` was true, `a[1].i` read null.\n\nTwo more defects surfaced in the probe, both present at HEAD:\n- an anon-typed index read came back as a plain I64, so `trace(arr[0])` printed the address and `Std.string(arr[0])` the number;\n- `trace(v)` for any anonymous object printed `null`: traceAny formats boxes, and the raw reference was passed unboxed (Std.string boxes it first).\n\nFix: pre-registration follows `return v` to a local object literal; anon-typed index reads load as pointers; trace boxes an anonymous object before traceAny. Probe/fixture: haxe-conformance/regressions/AnonReturnedThroughLocal.hx.","files":null}]}